    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0629" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/16543: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the President of the Chinese
                        Executive Yuan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Chiang Kai-shek</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-28">March 28, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I wish to express my appreciation of your telegram of March 18<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d653-f1"/> which contains an inspiring expression of the splendid
                    morale and confidence of the Chinese people. Their unimpaired spirit,
                    notwithstanding their burdens and sacrifices, stimulates and reinforces the
                    confidence of free peoples everywhere that with resolute determination and
                    cooperation on the part of those who are committed to it the cause of freedom
                    and justice will unquestionably prevail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin</hi> D. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
